NAME
    video - the video card: mirror the console on it, clear it

SYNOPSIS
    video [on | off | clear | init | probe]

DESCRIPTION
    The video card (an MC6845 CRTC and 2K of display RAM at $D000)
    is driven by the ROM (ROM 2026-09-25 and later). At reset the
    ROM tests $D000 and remembers whether the card answered; it does
    not start the card by itself until the card is debugged. video
    switches what the ROM does:

        video          status: the card found or not, mirroring, the
                       CRTC cursor, the text cursor's row and column
        video on       mirror the console on the screen: every byte
                       sent to the console (the ROM's CHAROUT) is
                       also written at the screen's cursor, so the
                       shell, its echo and every program show there
        video off      stop mirroring (the screen keeps its text)
        video clear    clear the screen, cursor to the top left
        video init     program the CRTC's registers, clear, home
                       (the monitor's V I); status afterwards
        video probe    test $D000 again; status afterwards

    The screen is 80 x 24 characters. CR, LF (a new line), BS, TAB
    and FF (clear) are obeyed; the text is upper-cased (the character
    ROM has 64 glyphs); the screen scrolls at the bottom.

    What goes to a > file or through a pipe is not console output and
    is not mirrored; error messages (the raw console) are.

    "video on" says "no video card at D000" when the ROM found none.
    On an older ROM video says "this ROM has no video driver" and
    changes nothing. video is /BIN/VIDEO.

EXAMPLES
    video            e.g.  video card found at D000, mirror off, ...
    video clear      then
    video on         the console from here on also on the screen

NOTES
    The flags are the ROM's: VIDPRES $0FF0, VIDMIR $0FF1; the entry
    $FFBC (VIDCTL) clears and initialises (see abi). Mirroring costs
    about 650 microcode steps a character. The monitor's V command
    does the same and more (V? lists it: write text, bytes, fill,
    dump the screen, CRTC registers).
    Written for Y1/OS 2026-09-25 (not in P8X).

SEE ALSO
    mon, abi
